    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/alma/jobs/5483169/assistant-or-associate-director-for-admissions-communications": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Director for Admissions Communications",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Job Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant or Associate Director for Admissions Communications  | Job Opportunities page has loaded. Assistant or Associate Director for Admissions Communications  | Job Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Job Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant or Associate Director for Admissions Communications Print Apply ﻿ Assistant or Associate Director for Admissions Communications Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Alma Job Type Staff - Full-Time Job Number 2026-00041 Division Enrollment Department Admissions Opening Date 09/15/2026 Closing Date 9/29/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Description Benefits POSITION SUMMARY The Assistant/Associate Director, in collaboration with the Communications and Marketing office and Senior Director of Admissions, will lead in the development, implementation, and execution of communications to support recruitment efforts. Communications include student recruitment communications, including print, email, text, presentation and other electronic . The Assistant/Associate Director will also develop communications and messaging for the Financial Aid Office, to both new and current students. The Assistant /Associate Director will take a direct role in content creation. Media used will be a broad variety of print, electronic, video, photo , email and text. Th is position will help coordinate undergraduate and graduate recruitment communications , as well as financial aid messaging and communication . The pos ition will attend Communications and Marketing planning meetings and collaborate extensively with t h e office in developing and disseminating communications. Salary and t itle commensurate with experience, skills, and abilities . Supervision Received/Exercised: This position reports to the Senior Director of Enrollment Systems and Operations and has no supervisory responsibilities. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Lead student recruitment communications initiatives from idea onto completion with a sense of urgency, working primarily independently and collaboratively to execute strategic communications. This role will: Independently manage timelines on multiple large-scale projects Research, review and develop content from a variety of sources Oversee, develop and implement annual Admissions communications, including publications, email and text campaigns, academic materials, and promotional materials(swag), in close collaboration with the Communications and Marketing office Develop, schedule and implement the day-to-day content for prospective students and supporters via the Customer Relationship Management ( CRM)A system, in collaboration with the Senior Director for Enrollment Systems and Operations Create and execute segmented communication plans that target all phases of the admissions funnel for prospective students and for key influencers Write, edit and coordinate targeted domestic and international communications and recruiting messages to prospective students, and high school and community college counselors Manage and coordinate variable content printing for on-demand print communication that includes writing, photo selection and partnering with an external vendor on printing Assist undergraduate and graduate admissions staff in editing and developing content for letters, emails, program invitations, tele-counseling phone scripts, advertisements, brochures, presentations, as well as managing communication and publication plans related to print, web, and recruitment events for various student audiences Coordinate the College chatbot in collaboration with the Senior Director for Enrollment Systems and Operations Develop and implement financial aid messaging and communications to both prospective and current students, in collaboration with the Director of Financial Aid Create, edit and maintain presentations for use by the Admissions and Financial Aid teams Create and implement special communication initiatives Manage the vendor delivery of Admissions recruitment material s and coor dinate wit h the Assista n t Dire ctor of En ro llm ent Sys tems and Oper ation s to en sure need ed materi als are always av ailable Other duties as assigned REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in English, Communication, Marketing or Higher Education Administration or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience Two years of experience in higher education recruitment, e-recruiting, marketing, or communication Familiarity with a CRM system Be proactive and have significant experience in writing and communication Excellent organizational and analytical skills Ability to work in a fast-paced work environment and manage multiple project deadlines simultaneously Highly organized and detail oriented Skilled at multitasking Ability to work within a team and independently Able to maintain confidentiality PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Communication , Higher Education Administration, Marketing or closely related field Experience in project management Experience working with undergraduate students and/or admissions/recruitment programs Alma College is classified as a selective Baccalaureate College: Diverse Fields by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching. Alma is committed to academic excellence and the development of responsible leaders; our students thrive on challenging academic programs in a supportive, small-college environment emphasizing active, collaborative learning and close student-faculty interaction. Alma is a private Phi Beta Kappa institution located in the center of Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. Alma College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse faculty, staff, and student body. Alma College recognizes that we are all transformed when we celebrate and value the varied identities, backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives in our campus community. We are committed to recognizing and removing barriers to success and providing equitable access to opportunities through education and advocacy. In our increasingly diverse campus and world, we pledge to create a climate where everyone is safe and free to grow intellectually, spiritually, and emotionally. We offer a comprehensive benefits package to employees in eligible positions working 30 hours or more per week. Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage; retirement plans; flexible spending accounts; life insurance; long-term disability; paid holidays; vacation; and sick leave. Part-time employees who average 20 hours per week over the course of a year are eligible for select benefits on a prorated basis. For additional details, please visit our Prospective Employees page. Employer Alma College (MI) Address 614 W. Superior St. Alma, Michigan, 48801 Phone 989-463-7467 Website https://www.alma.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells yo