      "description": "Job Opportunities | Job Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Systems Analyst | Job Opportunities page has loaded. Systems Analyst | Job Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Job Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Systems Analyst Print Apply ﻿ Systems Analyst Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Alma Job Type Staff - Full-Time Job Number 2026-00044 Division Business Affairs Department Information Technology Svcs Opening Date 09/15/2026 Closing Date 10/9/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Description Benefits POSITION SUMMARY The Systems Analyst supports Alma College's enterprise information systems (EIS), databases, reporting platforms, and data integrations. Working in collaboration with campus departments, vendors, and ITS staff, this position analyzes, improves, and helps modernize business processes, develops technical solutions, supports data-driven decision making, participates in enterprise systems and database administration activities, and helps ensure the effective operation, security, and long-term sustainability of the College's administrative systems. Supervision Received: This position reports to the Director of Web Development and has no supervisory responsibilities. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Enterprise Systems & Application Support Support the administration, maintenance, enhancement, and operation of enterprise applications including ERP, CRM, workflow management, reporting, and auxiliary systems. Assist with system implementations, upgrades, testing, troubleshooting, and vendor coordination. Develop, maintain, and support data integrations and information exchanges between institutional systems and third-party applications. Database Administration & Reporting ·Develop and maintain SQL queries, stored procedures, reports, dashboards, data extracts, and other reporting solutions that support departmental and institutional needs. Assist with database administration activities including performance monitoring, maintenance, security, data validation, and troubleshooting. Serve as an ITS representative for college-wide data governance, stewardship, reporting, and data quality initiatives. Analyze and interpret data to support informed business decision-making and operational effectiveness. Business Process Improvement & Department Collaboration Collaborate with departments, vendors, and ITS staff to build productive working relationships and deliver innovative process improvements based on an understanding of college business objectives. Translate business requirements into practical technical solutions through process redesign, automation, data integration, and system enhancements. Develop and maintain expertise in Alma College's core administrative systems while supporting user training, change management, documentation, communication, and knowledge-sharing efforts related to enterprise technologies. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in information technology, computer science, information systems, or related discipline Two years of professional experience supporting business systems, enterprise applications, databases, reporting, or related technologies Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Proficiency in writing and troubleshooting SQL queries Ability to analyze business processes and identify opportunities for improvement Excellent written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated ability to document technical and business processes clearly Ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical audiences Ability to learn complex enterprise software systems and institutional business processes PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working in higher education. Experience with Ellucian Colleague. Experience with Microsoft SQL Server. Experience supporting ERP, CRM, SIS, HR, Finance, or other enterprise systems. Experience with system integrations, APIs, and data exchanges. Experience with reporting, analytics, and document management systems. Experience with project coordination or project management methodologies. Experience working with underrepresented, first-generation, Pell-eligible, and diverse populations. Alma College is classified as a selective Baccalaureate College: Diverse Fields by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching. Alma is committed to academic excellence and the development of responsible leaders; our students thrive on challenging academic programs in a supportive, small-college environment emphasizing active, collaborative learning and close student-faculty interaction. Alma is a private Phi Beta Kappa institution located in the center of Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. Alma College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse faculty, staff, and student body. Alma College recognizes that we are all transformed when we celebrate and value the varied identities, backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives in our campus community. We are committed to recognizing and removing barriers to success and providing equitable access to opportunities through education and advocacy. In our increasingly diverse campus and world, we pledge to create a climate where everyone is safe and free to grow intellectually, spiritually, and emotionally. We offer a comprehensive benefits package to employees in eligible positions working 30 hours or more per week. Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage; retirement plans; flexible spending accounts; life insurance; long-term disability; paid holidays; vacation; and sick leave. Part-time employees who average 20 hours per week over the course of a year are eligible for select benefits on a prorated basis. For additional details, please visit our Prospective Employees page. Employer Alma College (MI) Address 614 W. Superior St. Alma, Michigan, 48801 Phone 989-463-7467 Website https://www.alma.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are c